# The Tailwind CLI and what it caches. Its own file rather than a line in the
# repository root's, because the toolchain arrives with this project and leaves
# with it (docs/architecture.md §3).
#
# The stylesheet it generates — `crates/app/style/sheet.css` — is deliberately not
# here and must never be: it is committed to the tree and compiled into the
# binary, which is what keeps `cargo run` free of Node
# (docs/adr/0003-the-stylesheet-is-generated-and-committed.md).
node_modules/

# What `just bundle-macos` writes: the application bundle and its disk image
# (docs/adr/0010-the-bundle-is-the-one-thing-dx-makes.md). An artifact, never
# a source.
dist/

# Cargo's output, and the rust-sdk checkout Testy is built from along with the
# binary (`just testy`, scripts/build-testy.sh). The repository root ignores
# both today; they are here as well so the ignore travels with the project when
# it splits out, for the same reason `node_modules/` is.
target/
.testy/

# devenv's own state: the evaluation cache and the profile links. Ignored at
# the host repository's root before the split, and here now for the same
# reason `target/` is — the ignore travels with the project.
.devenv/
.devenv.flake.nix
